  "method": "Isolated servers ran a real native-protocol player. The probe independently examined authoritative recipe slots, inputs, cursor and experience. The client independently decoded single-slot and full-container packet data, namespaced item model, material, count, original name/lore, leading Recipe locked line, exact system-chat text, optional fallback and return to the original empty slot. Native packet checks used PrismarineJS or the official 26.2 and 26.3 registry reports.",
  "coverage": [
    "Player crafting and a full workbench, virtual anvil transformation and damage repair, smithing preparation, result-slot and chat combinations, silent mode and optional-dependency fallback.",
    "Ordinary registered recipes yielded genuine denied empty-result clicks. Two separate controlled removal-of-native-registration cases forced the ordinary InventoryClickEvent on both player crafting and workbench while the managed catalog retained its rule.",
    "Unrelated registered lookalike, real permission grants, late click cancellation, changed inputs/windows/revisions/permissions and foreign nonempty smithing result.",
    "Actual clicks on transient client-only markers and successful allowed results; denied server cursor, ingredients and experience audited independently."
